{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The rider did what the platform asks a rider to do: she read the driver's 11:58:28 message ('hi im at the pickup point, where are you') and answered it at 12:00:23 with 'coming down now'. The driver sent no further message and the record shows no in-app voice call at any point (trip_record.in_app_calls is empty), so under POL-NS-04 limbs (a) and (b) the rider's locating message went unanswered for the 270 seconds that remained and the driver terminated at 12:04:53 without ever replying to her or calling her. I do not put limb (c) forward as met — the rider track places her device about 645 m from the pin, outside the 100 m STANDARD presence radius — so POL-NS-04 is not automatic exoneration here; the point is that the driver's own silence is a driver-side coordination failure that the ruling, and any escalation packet, should record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-03302", "EV-TRIP-03302", "EV-GPS-03302"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Both profiles report one no-show dispute with a counterparty in the trailing 90 days — rider_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d = 1 and driver_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d = 1 — and the rider and driver on this trip are the two parties those counters describe. Read together, as POL-NS-09(c) directs, they show 2 no-show disputes between the same rider and driver in the trailing 90 days, which meets the clause's '2 or more', so escalation to human review is mandatory on this record rather than optional. Under POL-GEN-03 escalation is terminal: no monetary ruling issues and the disputed $4.50 is held rather than collected or refunded, so the rider is not left carrying a no-show fee that a human reviewer has not yet confirmed.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-03302", "EV-DPROF-03302"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-GEN-01 permits only the profile fields a clause names to ground a finding. The rider's lifetime prior_no_show_flags counter (1) and her rating (4.71) are context only and may never be read against her; the only rider no-show counter any clause reads is rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d, and POL-NS-09(d) treats that counter as a signal only at 3 or more. At 1, nothing on her profile can carry an adverse finding on this trip or be used to justify leaving the charge in place.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-03302"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-01", "POL-NS-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "EV-ADVIS-03302-01 is MISSING: no traffic advisory covers the pickup at Blk 640 Jurong West St 61 in this window, the artifact carries weight_multiplier 0.0 and the issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, and under POL-GEN-02 a weight-0.0 artifact can carry no fact while the absence itself is citable. POL-NS-06(i) allows a driver to accumulate dwell across separate in-geofence intervals only where a populated advisory of an admissible type covers the pickup road, so that limb is unavailable on this record, and nothing in the bundle identifies any kerbside restriction that kept the driver from the pin.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-03302-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.accumulated_dwell.limb.available",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    }
  ]
}
